 "notes": "Headline bound from Eq.(39): post-inflation PQ-breaking misalignment overclosure bound fa <= (4.10 +/- 0.04)e11 GeV, equivalently ma >= (14.6 +/- 0.1) ueV, derived from the paper's pure-glue SU(3) lattice topological susceptibility fitted to the DIGM and Planck Omega_DM h^2 = 0.1199 (Eq.38). Curve is the QCD-axion line segment (paper's Eq.(3) relation, m_a*f_a = sqrt(mu*md)/(mu+md)*m_pi*f_pi, so 1/fa = 2.439e-12 GeV^-1 x (m/14.6 ueV)) over the excluded masses m <= 14.6 ueV, ending exactly at the quoted bound point (1.46e-5 eV, 2.439e-12 GeV^-1); the low-mass end at 1e-8 eV is an arbitrary plotting cutoff. Cosmological (relic-density) bound, so no local DM density rescaling applied. The paper quotes 1-sigma-style errors and states no explicit CL; 0.95 entered as schema default. Caveat noted by the authors: pure Yang-Mills (no dynamical quarks), misalignment only (strings/domain walls would tighten it).",
